<title>USA: GOLF-LEADING SCORES FROM COLORADO.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING SCORES FROM COLORADO.</headline>
<dateline>CASTLE ROCK, Colorado 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores</p>
<p>after the first round at the $1.7 million Sprint International</p>
<p>golf tournament on the 7,559-yard, par-72 Castle Pines course</p>
<p>(players U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>(The tournament is played under a modified stable format</p>
<p>that awards five points for eagle, two for birdie, zero for</p>
<p>par, and subtracts one point for bogey, three points for</p>
<p>double bogey or worse. Seventy two players were unable to</p>
<p>complete round due to bad weather.)</p>
<p>15-Larry Mize</p>
<p>14-Phil Mickelson</p>
<p>12-Dave Stockton, Jr</p>
<p>11-Scott McCarron</p>
<p>10-Olin Browne, Brad Faxon, Dudley Hart, Hideki Kase (Japan)</p>
<p>9-Stewart Cink</p>
<p>8-Tommy Armour, Neal Lancaster, Jimmy Green, Grant Waite</p>
<p>(New Zealand)</p>
<p>7-Ted Tryba, Steve Stricker</p>
<p>6-Rick Fehr, Craig Stadler, Robin Freeman, Taylor Smith</p>
<p>5-Retief Goosen (South Africa), Peter Lonard (Australia),</p>
<p>Davis Love, Ernie Els (South Africa)</p>
<p>Additional regional scores:</p>
<p>0-Nick Faldo (Britain)</p>
<p>-2-Brad Hughes (Australia), Mike Weir (Canada)</p>
</text>
